  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "Spanish uses reflexive clitic pronouns with certain verbs to emphasise that the subject consumes or does something completely. Expressions like *comerse* (to eat up) and *beberse* (to drink up) stress that the whole item has been consumed. In these cases, the reflexive pronoun precedes the object pronoun (e.g., *me lo tomé*)."
    }
